From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anxelok <anxelok@localhost>
Date: Fri, 19 Jun 2026 19:28:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Re-enter compatibility apartment on same-thread ownership
 alone
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The per-plugin compatibility apartment keyed re-entrancy on (ownerThread,
transactionId). A plugin that synchronously fires its OWN event from inside one
of its listeners (a nested callEvent, a NEW transaction on the SAME thread) hit
BUSY and was REFUSED, even though a single thread cannot race itself. This is
exactly WorldGuard: its listener on a Bukkit CreatureSpawnEvent / BlockPlaceEvent
/ BlockBreakEvent fires WG's own delegate (SpawnEntityEvent / PlaceBlockEvent /
BreakBlockEvent) via Bukkit.getPluginManager().callEvent(); the delegate's
region-protection listeners then hit the same-thread BUSY refusal and never run,
silently bypassing place/break/spawn protection under parallel ticking
(transient_refusal: SpawnEntity x396, PlaceBlock x40, BreakBlock x40 in the
compat corpus — all same-thread nested re-entries, zero cross-thread).

Match re-entrancy on thread identity alone. The apartment is per-plugin, so a
thread already holding the lease that re-enters is always the plugin's own
synchronous nested call. Safe (no data race) and correct (plugin re-entering
itself); the cross-thread BUSY path (the apartment's actual cross-thread
serialization purpose) is unchanged.


diff --git a/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/plugin/manager/compat/CompatibilityApartment.java b/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/plugin/manager/compat/CompatibilityApartment.java
index 8bd9acfc677a854a19bf3e5b88473f0ad27120ef..63009af5233851977b4bb84099b8de84e9e7a2e7 100644
--- a/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/plugin/manager/compat/CompatibilityApartment.java
+++ b/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/plugin/manager/compat/CompatibilityApartment.java
@@ -102,7 +102,20 @@ public final class CompatibilityApartment {
                 continue;
             }
 
-            if (current.ownerThread == currentThread && current.transactionId == transactionId) {
+            // Loom Fix 1d - re-enter on SAME-THREAD ownership alone, regardless of transactionId. This apartment
+            // is per-plugin, so a thread that already holds this plugin's lease and re-enters is ALWAYS the
+            // plugin's own synchronous, nested call — never a concurrent contender (a single thread cannot race
+            // itself). The previous `&& current.transactionId == transactionId` guard only re-entered the SAME
+            // event's re-dispatch and treated a NESTED dispatch of a DIFFERENT event as foreign contention. That
+            // is exactly the WorldGuard pattern: WG's listener on a Bukkit event (e.g. CreatureSpawnEvent /
+            // BlockPlaceEvent / BlockBreakEvent) synchronously fires WG's own delegate event (SpawnEntityEvent /
+            // PlaceBlockEvent / BreakBlockEvent) via Bukkit.getPluginManager().callEvent() from inside that
+            // listener. The delegate is a fresh transaction, so under the old guard the nested dispatch hit BUSY
+            // on the same thread and was REFUSED — so WG's region-protection listeners on the delegate never ran,
+            // silently bypassing place/break/spawn protection under parallel ticking. Matching on thread identity
+            // alone is both safe (same thread, no data race) and correct (it is the plugin re-entering itself),
+            // and leaves the cross-thread BUSY path (the apartment's actual purpose) unchanged.
+            if (current.ownerThread == currentThread) {
                 current.depth.incrementAndGet();
                 final CompatibilityRuntimeContext.Scope context = transaction == null
                     ? CompatibilityRuntimeContext.enter(this.plugin, transactionId, strictFallback, path)
diff --git a/src/test/java/io/papermc/paper/plugin/manager/compat/CompatibilityApartmentTest.java b/src/test/java/io/papermc/paper/plugin/manager/compat/CompatibilityApartmentTest.java
index ed1d500b0398b32135926e234045cbdafccf6422..c1b9987c7f63f6b0fde0845a8b12d00e62016c80 100644
--- a/src/test/java/io/papermc/paper/plugin/manager/compat/CompatibilityApartmentTest.java
+++ b/src/test/java/io/papermc/paper/plugin/manager/compat/CompatibilityApartmentTest.java
@@ -39,6 +39,32 @@ class CompatibilityApartmentTest {
         }
     }
 
+    @Test
+    void sameThreadNestedDifferentTransactionReenters() {
+        // Loom Fix 1d regression - a thread that already holds this plugin's lease re-enters even when the
+        // nested dispatch is a DIFFERENT transaction (the WorldGuard pattern: a listener synchronously fires the
+        // plugin's own delegate event, a fresh transaction, from inside the current one). This must be REENTRANT,
+        // not BUSY, or WorldGuard's region-protection listeners on the delegate would be refused and its
+        // place/break/spawn protection silently bypassed.
+        final Plugin plugin = mockPlugin("LegacyPlugin");
+        final CompatibilityApartment apartment = new CompatibilityApartment(plugin);
+        final CompatibilityTransaction outer = transactionFor(plugin);
+        final CompatibilityTransaction nested = transactionFor(plugin);
+        Assertions.assertNotEquals(outer.id(), nested.id(), "the nested dispatch must be a distinct transaction");
+
+        try (CompatibilityApartment.Scope outerScope = apartment.enter(outer, false)) {
+            Assertions.assertEquals(CompatibilityApartment.EnterResult.ACQUIRED, outerScope.result());
+            try (CompatibilityApartment.Scope nestedScope = apartment.enter(nested, false)) {
+                Assertions.assertEquals(CompatibilityApartment.EnterResult.REENTRANT, nestedScope.result());
+                Assertions.assertTrue(nestedScope.acquired());
+            }
+            // After the nested scope closes the outer lease must still be held (depth bookkeeping).
+            try (CompatibilityApartment.Scope stillHeld = apartment.enter(outer, false)) {
+                Assertions.assertEquals(CompatibilityApartment.EnterResult.REENTRANT, stillHeld.result());
+            }
+        }
+    }
+
     @Test
     void strictFallbackExecutorRunsSerializedTasks() {
         final Plugin plugin = mockPlugin("LegacyPlugin");
